3. The right of Victims to Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b includes:
a. provision of information regarding rights and Protection facilities;
b. provision of access to information on the implementation of Protection;
c. protection from threats or violence by perpetrators and other parties as well as recurrence of violence;
d. protection of identity confidentiality;
e. protection from attitudes and behavior of law enforcement officials that demean Victims;
f. protection from loss of employment, job transfer, Education, or political access; and
g. protection of Victims and/or reporters from criminal prosecution or civil lawsuits for Crimes of Sexual Violence that have been reported.
4. The right of Victims to recovery as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c includes:
a. medical rehabilitation;
b. mental and social rehabilitation;
c. social empowerment;
d. restitution and/or compensation;
e. social reintegration; and
f. obtaining skills training for economic improvement for vulnerable women.

Article 12

1. Empowerment of Women victims of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination is carried out in an integrated manner in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
2. Empowerment of Women victims of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination as referred to in paragraph (1) is directed to obtain opportunities and rights as human beings to be able to play a role and participate in activities:
a. health;
b. education;
c. economy;
d. law;
e. manpower;
f. politics;
g. government;
h. social affairs;
i. culture; and
j. environment.

MAYOR OF SURAKARTA

CENTRAL JAVA PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SURAKARTA CITY NUMBER 7 OF 2024

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD THE MAYOR OF SURAKARTA,

COPY

Considering:
a. that women are citizens who have human rights that must be protected, respected, maintained, and may not be neglected, reduced, or deprived by anyone, thus requiring protection guarantees from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;
b. that in order to realize the fulfillment of women's constitutional rights to be free from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination, as well as to improve the quality of life of women, they need to receive protection and empowerment from the Regional Government;
c. that the implementation of protection of women in the Region has not been able to be carried out optimally and is accompanied by the continued occurrence of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women, thus requiring a comprehensive regulation to provide direction, foundation, and legal certainty;

2 -
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 16 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Large City Regions Within the Province of East Java, Central Java, West Java and the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 45);
