1. Services are carried out to fulfill the rights of women victims conducted with the following principles:
a. respect for human rights;
b. non-discrimination;
c. confidentiality;
d. empathy;
e. inclusion;
f. empowerment;
g. decisions based on the victim;
h. honesty;
i. professionalism;
j. integration; and
k. sustainability.
2. The provision of services to victims is carried out in an integrated manner by UPTD PPA.
3. In the provision of services as referred to in paragraph (1), UPTD PPA may cooperate with:
a. community health centers, hospitals, and other health service facilities;
b. technical implementing units in charge of affairs in the social field;
c. detention centers, correctional institutions, and correctional centers;
d. police;
e. prosecutor's office;
f. courts;
g. technical implementing units of agencies that administer the protection of migrant workers;
h. provincial regional offices of ministries that administer governmental affairs in the field of religion;

23 -
i. regional offices and technical implementing units of Ministries that administer governmental affairs in the field of law and human rights;
j. regional representatives of the Witness and Victim Protection Agency;
k. social welfare organizing institutions;
l. community-based service provider institutions; and
m. other institutions.

Article 19

The Implementation of Women's Empowerment in the social field as referred to in Article 12 paragraph (2) letter h shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the social field and other related agencies in the form of:
a. awareness-raising and self-capacity enhancement in the social field;
b. provision and development of access for women to participate in the social field;
c. enhancement of women's competence through training and social education for women;
d. involvement of women in social activities; and
e. cultivation and development of women's forums or institutions in the social field.

