f. providing legal services;
g. identifying economic empowerment needs;
h. identifying temporary shelter needs for Victims and Victims' Families that need to be fulfilled immediately;
i. facilitating the needs of Victims with Disabilities;
j. coordinating and working together on the fulfillment of Victims' rights with other institutions; and - 32 -
k. monitoring the fulfillment of Victims' rights by law enforcement apparatus during the judicial process.
