Article 6

1. The forms of Violence referred to in Article 5 include:a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic violence;
e. exploitation; andf. KBGO.

16 - (2) Economic Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d includes:
a. taking full control over the victim's income, including salary, savings, or other financial assistance received by the victim:b. restricting or prohibiting the victim from owning or using money, so that the victim is completely dependent on the perpetrator for financial needs:c. prohibiting or preventing the victim from working or continuing education with the aim of limiting the victim's financial independence:d. using the victim's assets or property for personal gain or damaging such assets as a form of punishment; ande. making all financial decisions without involving the victim, so that the victim has no control over household finances.
3. Exploitation as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e at a minimum:a. exploiting women's labor by providing inadequate wages, imposing excessive working hours, or not providing safe and healthy working conditions;
b. exploiting women for sexual purposes, by coercion, deception, or pressure. Including human trafficking for the purpose of prostitution or pornography production; andc. exploiting women unfairly in economic transactions, such as providing loans with very high interest or manipulating the market for personal gain.
4. KBGO as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f, includes:a. comments or messages that are insulting, demeaning, or belittling women;

17 -
b. messages or comments that threaten to commit physical or sexual violence against women;
c. disseminating the victim's personal information (such as address, telephone number, or other identity) without permission with the aim of intimidating or harming the victim;
d. extortion involving threats to spread intimate images or videos of the victim unless the victim meets the perpetrator's demands;
e. spreading private photos or videos of an intimate nature without the consent of the woman in the content;
f. use of technology to stalk or monitor the victim continuously, often with the aim of frightening or controlling the victim; andg. digitally altering images or videos of women for the purpose of insulting, humiliating, or sexually exploiting.

Article 9

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in Article 8, is carried out by Regional Apparatus that administer governmental affairs in the fields of:
a. health;
b. education;
c. manpower;
d. cooperatives, small and medium enterprises and industry;
e. social affairs;
f. communication and informatics;
g. culture;
h. tourism;
i. environment;
j. transportation;
k. trade;
l. youth and sports;
m. politics;
n. public tranquility, order, and community protection;
o. public works and spatial planning;
p. public housing and residential areas;
q. women's empowerment and child protection;
r. population administration and civil registration;
s. population control and family planning; and
t. other related fields.
2. Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Women's Protection and Empowerment.

