Part Two

Prevention of Violence, Exploitation and Discrimination ArticIe 8 (1) The Regional Government carries out efforts to prevent violence, exploitation and discrimination against women in an integrated manner in the Region.

2. The prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women is intended to create a safe environment for women and to reduce the vulnerability to violence, exploitation and discrimination of vulnerable women groups.
3. Vulnerable women groups as referred to in paragraph (2) include:a. women in disaster and social conflict situations;
b. women with disabilities; c. women with HIV/AIDS;
d. women migrant workers;
e. women heads of households;
f. women domestic workers;
g. women home-based workers;
h. elderly women;
i. women informal workers;
j. women in situations of intolerance; and k. other vulnerable women groups.
4. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are implemented by:a. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of the prevention of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination based on partnership patterns;
b. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women's rights;
c. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system for the prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination;

19 -
d. providing easy access to obtain civil rights, education, health, employment, training and funding, welfare improvement and services;
e. developing media for communication, information, education and public campaigns through media; f. developing educational materials and curricula;
g. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
h. building early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential areas, educational environments, Islamic boarding schools and other public spaces;
i. providing consultation services for families, prospective brides and grooms, students, Islamic students, youth, university students and vulnerable groups;
j. encouraging behavioral change of parents and the community;
k. developing policies related to regencies/cities, sub-districts, schools, Islamic boarding schools, and universities that are safe and friendly for women and integrated with regional spatial planning policies;
l. forming and developing cadres, communities, and groups from among youth, students, Islamic students, university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, and religious leaders for prevention;
m. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or users of social media; n. developing protection systems and special support for vulnerable women groups;
o. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;

20 -
p. increasing the capacity of Regional Apparatus, government agencies, educational institutions, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, business sector, service institutions, Islamic boarding schools, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, media, religious leaders, community leaders and communities; andq. forming cooperation networks in prevention efforts from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination with law enforcement apparatus, government agencies, Regional Apparatus, community institutions, educational institutions, community leaders, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, business sector, service institutions, Islamic boarding schools, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, communities, and media.
5. Efforts to prevent Violence, Exploitation and Discrimination against women in an integrated manner as referred to in paragraph (1) are coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection as well as governmental affairs in the field of population control and family planning.
6. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (3) letter a may involve Regional Apparatus, agencies, community institutions, educational institutions, community leaders, integrated service posts, family learning centers, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, business sector, service institutions, Islamic boarding schools, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, communities, and media.

